==Battleground==
*50 [[Shibalien Elite]]s (400%) spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Shibalien Elite]] (10%) spawns as the boss.
**4 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn, delay 14.67~22 seconds<sup>440f~660f</sup>.
**4 [[Scissoroo]]s spawn, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is balanced around maxed [[anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] from [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 2, with which it is relatively easy. If you have them from Chapter 3 as well, it's a pushover.

To stall the Shibaliens at the beginning, stall with 4 meatshields and [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]]. Use [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] too, but never, under most circumstances, use more than two if you are stalling. After the Shibaliens are killed, use mid-ranged attackers such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] to deal direct damage while [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] such as [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] and [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] paralyze the melee pushers. General GreGory's [[Barrier]] is weak enough for [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breakers]] to be unnecessary. Once the main threats have been eliminated, just push to the base and the stage is easily won.

